## Overview

Dual rendering: **Rendered LaTeX View** (KaTeX math, dark theme on screen, white for PDFs) and **Raw Text View** (plain text, dark theme). All rendering flows through `LatexRenderer.jsx` (`frontend/src/components/LatexRenderer.jsx`). CSS in `LatexRenderer.css`. PDF generation via `downloadHelpers.js`.

**Performance Architecture**: Paper views and the Autonomous brainstorm viewer default to rendered mode, including large documents; the brainstorm checkbox stays adjacent to its label. Math-aware chunks preserve complete source and protected constructs. A bounded cancellable dedicated worker handles conversion, with main-thread sanitization before publication. Viewport windowing and offscreen HTML eviction limit retained rendered content; live snapshots have bounded latency and document-identity fences. Oversized or failed atomic blocks expose complete raw source and explicit recovery rather than synchronous unbounded conversion. Responsiveness claims require measured browser tests, not character-count guarantees.

### Props API

```javascript
<LatexRenderer
  content={string}       // Raw content to render
  documentId={string}    // Stable document identity, separate from content revision
  className={string}     // Optional CSS class
  showToggle={boolean}   // Show Rendered/Raw toggle (default: true)
  defaultRaw={boolean}   // Start in raw mode (default: false)
  showLatex={boolean}    // External view mode control (optional)
/>
```

