## Rendering Pipeline (CRITICAL ORDER)

The raw conversion inside `renderLatexToHtml()` may include targeted preprocessing repairs between these anchors. Preserve these order constraints rather than treating every intermediate fix as a rule-level invariant:

1. **`decodeHtmlEntities()`** — FIRST
2. Apply renderer-specific text/LaTeX repairs and auto-wrap unwrapped math before theorem/section/text formatting
3. **`processTheoremEnvironments()`** — TikZ handling happens before KaTeX (all three patterns: `\[...\]`, `$$...$$`, standalone)
4. **KaTeX rendering** via `renderKatexSafely()` — `maxExpand: 5000`, skips HTML placeholder content
5. **Line breaks/horizontal rules** (`\\` → `<br/>`, `\hrule` → `<hr/>`) — AFTER KaTeX

DOMPurify sanitization remains outside the conversion function and mandatory before every screen HTML sink and PDF payload publication.

**Critical:** `\\` line break conversion MUST be after KaTeX (valid syntax in `aligned`, `matrix`, etc.)

### Chunked Rendering Architecture

**Chunking**: Split only outside protected math, environment, brace, and code boundaries; concatenated chunks must reproduce the original source. Macro-definition-bearing sources remain atomic to preserve ordered same-document definitions without cross-document worker leakage. Large atomic constructs require explicit safe handling, never blind character splitting.

**Virtualization**: Nearby chunks render on demand; measured-height placeholders preserve scroll geometry outside the viewport window. Live-paper toolbar checkboxes keep fixed unpadded native geometry across focus changes so mouse presses cannot move adjacent download targets. Focused/selected content is protected during interaction. Complete source remains available in raw view and exports; rendered browser search/selection and direct-print limitations must be visible.

**Live updates**: Bounded-latency snapshots avoid trailing-debounce starvation. Stable block identity is separate from content revision, and stale document/worker results cannot replace current content.

**Viewer lifecycle requirements**: Background refreshes and unrelated parent renders must retain the mounted reader. Polling/live-event demand must not indefinitely invalidate successful in-flight reads. All content/outline publishers must be fenced to current document/session and clear/unmount ownership; exports must use matching content and identity. Enabled auto-follow must track asynchronous rendered layout changes; disabled auto-follow must preserve the reading position.

**Audit status**: The brainstorm API-wrapper remount fix is implemented. Slow-request starvation in brainstorm/live Tier 2/Tier 3 readers, stale publication in PaperLibrary/manual LivePaper, and auto-follow timing remain identified implementation gaps—not completed guarantees. Verify fixes with delayed/out-of-order/clear regressions and real-browser scroll checks; mocked DOM retention alone does not establish scroll stability.

**Large-document threshold**: Documents >50K chars (`LARGE_DOC_THRESHOLD`) use the same progressive chunk rendering while preserving the caller's selected/default view.

**Invariant**: Each chunk independently runs `renderLatexToHtml()` and then `DOMPurify.sanitize()`. Chunked and single-document paths must share the same conversion helpers and ordering anchors.

